Derived work
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of utina are derived from bakobo/thesmo (https://github.com/bakobo/thesmo),
Copyright 2026 Bakobo, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

thesmo is a deliberately blind implementation of the Custos specification: its
implementers read the ratified specification and nothing else, so that where two
independent readings disagree, the disagreement is evidence about the document
rather than about the readers. utina is not blind and makes no such claim. Where
utina carries a reading pinned by thesmo, it carries it because that reading is
defensible, not because it was independently derived here.

Specific provenance is recorded per module in the source. As of this writing:

  - The finding codomain, the closed appraisal triple, the transition system and
    the two upward currents derive from thesmo's `m1-alpha` reading of the
    finding-codomain chapter.
  - The byte-canonical encoding derives from thesmo's `m1-beta` reading.
  - The canonical-order log walk derives, as an algorithm rather than as source,
    from thesmo's `m2-gamma` reading of the GEL grammar chapter.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specifications implemented, not redistributed
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Custos (https://github.com/Nicholas-Keystate/custos) is licensed by its author
under the Community Specification License 1.0. utina implements it. No part of
the specification text is redistributed here; citations in comments and
documentation identify spans by line for the reader's benefit.

The ACDC and CESR specifications are likewise implemented or referenced rather
than redistributed.

Two specifications are the exception, and for the same reason.

The KERI specification (https://github.com/trustoverip/kswg-keri-specification).
schemas/keri-spec-body.md is a verbatim copy of that repository's
spec/spec-body.md at commit 71cb54ebb445dd9d8cb33cd29a5f50894fafc569, the
Key Event Receipt Infrastructure (KERI) specification at that revision,
redistributed unmodified because utina's law pins it by the SHA-256 of exactly
those bytes and the test suite recomputes the digest. It is Copyright 2023 KERI
Contributors and licensed under the OWFa 1.0, as stated in that repository's
LICENSE.md; that license, not this repository's, governs the file.

The dossier specification (https://github.com/trustoverip/kswg-dossier-specification).
schemas/dossier-spec-body.md is a verbatim copy of that
repository's spec/dossier-spec-body.md at commit
5906e8cf570099761b57761fac6cbec50325b3c1, redistributed unmodified because
utina's law pins its semantics by the SHA-256 of exactly those bytes and the
test suite recomputes the digest. The copied file carries no notice of its own.
The upstream specification, of which it is the body, is subject to the OWF
Contributor License Agreement 1.0 - Copyright, as stated in that repository's
spec/dossier-spec-head.md; that license, not this repository's, governs the
file.
